<h1 class="font-semibold text-4xl text-slate-600">Filter Feed By iTunes Season</h1>

<p>The McElroy's are very good about separating each arc using an iTunes season.</p>

<ol>
<li>
  Find the RSS feed.<br/>
  The RSS feed is usually under the "Subscribe" option of a podcast and can be found with the RSS icon: <span class="bg-orange rounded"><i class="text-white fa-solid fa-rss p-1"></span></i>
</li>
<li>Copy the RSS link and save it for later.</li>
<li>From the Minicast dashboard, select "Add New Podcast".</li>
<li>Give the main feed a title and add the RSS URL.
  <img src="/img/features/taz-add-new-podcast.png" alt="The UI for adding the podcast name and feed URL for The Adventure Zone" />
</li>
<li>Load the podcast and select "Add New Mini Cast".</li>
<li>Give the mini cast a title, select the season you want, and add a poster image for your podcast player.
  <img src="/img/features/taz-mini-feed-details.png" alt="The UI for adding mini feed details, here concentrating on the iTunes season." />
</li>
<li>Add the mini feed URL to your podcast player and enjoy.
  <img src="/img/features/taz-mini-feed-url.png" width="200" alt="The location of the mini feed URL on the minicast dashboard." />
</li>
